    "post_rendered": "USe the lemma <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e82f5ae6006ea396d3b096c50f19ea5bb3355e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^m+2^m+..(p-1)^m \\equiv 0 (mod p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" > for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"8\" > satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/d/f4d1f8f69f9c363f1cd10b0362a43f58e3b4f5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq m \\leq (p-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" > <img src=\"/assets/images/smilies/smile.gif\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\":)\" title=\":)\" class=\"bbcode_smiley\" />  <img src=\"/assets/images/smilies/smile.gif\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" alt=\":)\" title=\":)\" class=\"bbcode_smiley\" />",
    "post_canonical": "USe the lemma $1^m+2^m+..(p-1)^m \\equiv 0 (mod p)$ for all $m$ satisfies $0 \\leq m \\leq (p-2)$ :)  :)",
