    "topic_id": 42565,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Let <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1979ad6aac0d50e91dbfa17781687008e53e5f7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2, n \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" >,</span> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9264bf2fe914c02c8c7e56a353235c9ca2a83fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/b/26bdeb6802fe58097e71a90afa04ebbb5ab24830.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{c}{d} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"33\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3ef083c7ccc5509639530f3f767746ab0eb488d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + c \\leq n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" > find the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/f/1af93037a72bc44e076c250a88274ac50cb955b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" > for fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"8\" >",
    "post_canonical": "Let $n \\geq 2, n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, $a,b,c,d \\in \\mathbb{N}$, $\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{c}{d} < 1$ and $a + c \\leq n,$ find the maximum value of $\\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{c}{d}$ for fixed $n.$",
