    "post_rendered": "Let <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59cf4613fc4a578afcbce252c6839a4a4c23dfe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{(x,y) | x = 1, 2, \\ldots, 1993, y = 1, 2, 3, 4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"341\" height=\"18\" >.</span> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baac0f4d79e78b2ce11633b027811ca1ad2ff660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\subset S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" > and there aren't any squares in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e429d0525390a2f39aff76b978aa88336056b732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T.$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > Find the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/860d4496cc2e0459a95d70188c7365d96983a653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" > The squares in T use points in S as vertices.",
